How to run this project
Open terminals:
    Terminal 1 - php artisan serve              (Web Server)    -   Starts the app at http://127.0.0.1:8000                        
    Terminal 2 - php artisan reverb:start       (WebSocket Server(Real-time))   -   Powers live inventory updates and message notifications
    Terminal 3 - php artisan queue:work         (Queue Worker (Broadcasting))   -   Processes background jobs (sending notifications when pharmacy status changes)
    Terminal 4 - npm run dev                    (Vite (Frontend assets - only needed if editing the CSS/JS))    -   Skip this if you're not making frontend changes

# Terminal 1 - Laravel App
php artisan serve --host=127.0.0.1 --port=8000

# Terminal 2 - Reverb WebSocket
php artisan reverb:start --host=127.0.0.1 --port=8080

# Terminal 3 - Nginx (optional)
cd C:\nginx; .\nginx.exe


One-time setup steps (only needed if running on a fresh machine):
# Install PHP dependencies
composer install
# Install JS dependencies
npm install
# Copy environment file
copy .env.example .env
# Generate app key
php artisan key:generate
# Run database migrations
php artisan migrate
# Create storage symlink (for pharmacy logos)
php artisan storage:link


Checklist before opening the browser:
    PostgreSQL is running on port 5432
    .env has correct DB_PASSWORD set to root123
    Terminals 1, 2, and 3 are all running
    Open http://127.0.0.1:8000



